{"kind":"grammar","lang":"en","entities":{"n4-901":{"renderings":[{"id":"84386186d1f52acf","role":"label","field":"name","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n4-901"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"Volitional"},{"id":"d3f7a3fe273ff6b0","role":"prose","field":"shortExplanation","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n4-901"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"The plain 'let's / I think I'll' form, the casual counterpart of ましょう."},{"id":"6c0ae1d28000d0fc","role":"prose","field":"longExplanation","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n4-901"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"The volitional expresses intention or invitation in casual speech, and is the base of よう と思う ('I think I'll') and よう にする ('make an effort to')."},{"id":"b872957fa05ae2a6","role":"prose","field":"formation","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n4-901"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"Godan shift to the お-row + う (書く -> 書こう, 買う -> 買おう); ichidan drop る + よう (食べる -> 食べよう); する -> しよう, 来る -> 来よう."},{"id":"306029082b4f27b9","role":"label","field":"derives","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n4-901"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"volitional (よう / let's)"}]}}}